  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfrac></math> and the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mtext>min</mtext><mo>{</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>}</mo><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mtext> and </mtext><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>. Then",
    "image": null
  },
